{% comment %}
  The country list the location picker shows — rendered twice, once in the
  desktop drawer and once inside the mobile menu, so the two never drift.

  TWO LEVELS, on the owner's word (8 Sep 2026): "I don't want every country
  in the world listed." The store sells to 215 countries, most of them
  through the International market, and a list of 215 is not a choice, it
  is a scroll. So the first level is the countries the owner names —
  Theme settings → Location picker → "Countries listed by name", the
  countries of the eleven markets plus Mexico, Norway and Switzerland — and
  one row more, "Rest of world", which opens the second level: every other
  country, with a filter above it because that is the long one. Where the
  visitor's own country is a rest-of-world one, the row says so beside the
  words, and carries the current mark, so they can see where they are
  without opening it.

  A country is a BUTTON rather than a link: the click sets the localization
  form's country and submits it, and there is no page a link could honestly
  point at. What the row prints is Shopify's own name for the country, in
  the language the visitor is reading. With the setting left empty the
  first level is every country and there is no second — the shape the
  picker had before the rule.

  Accepts: suffix — a short word making the ids unique per render.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign suffix = suffix | default: 'list'
  assign current_iso = localization.country.iso_code
  assign named_raw = settings.location_named_countries | default: '' | upcase | strip_newlines | replace: ' ', ''
  assign named = named_raw | split: ','
  assign rest_count = 0
  assign current_in_rest = false
  if named_raw != ''
    for c in localization.available_countries
      unless named contains c.iso_code
        assign rest_count = rest_count | plus: 1
        if c.iso_code == current_iso
          assign current_in_rest = true
        endif
      endunless
    endfor
  endif
-%}
<div class="st-location__list" data-location-list data-level="all">
  <ul class="st-location__countries st-location__level st-location__level--all" role="list">
    {%- for c in localization.available_countries -%}
      {%- if named_raw == '' or named contains c.iso_code -%}
        <li class="st-location__item">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="st-location__country{% if c.iso_code == current_iso %} is-current{% endif %}"
            data-location-pick="{{ c.iso_code }}"
            data-market="{{ c.market.handle }}"
            {% if c.iso_code == current_iso %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
          >{{ c.name }}</button>
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if rest_count > 0 -%}
      <li class="st-location__item">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="st-location__country st-location__more{% if current_in_rest %} is-current{% endif %}"
          data-location-level="rest"
          aria-expanded="false"
          aria-controls="StLocationRest-{{ suffix }}"
          {% if current_in_rest %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
        ><span>{{ 'localization.rest_of_world' | t }}<span data-location-rest-name>{% if current_in_rest %} &middot; {{ localization.country.name }}{% endif %}</span></span><span class="st-location__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button>
      </li>
    {%- endif -%}
  </ul>
  {%- if rest_count > 0 -%}
    <div class="st-location__level st-location__level--rest" id="StLocationRest-{{ suffix }}">
      <button type="button" class="st-location__country st-location__back" data-location-level="all"><span class="st-location__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&larr;</span>{{ 'localization.all_locations' | t }}</button>
      <label class="st-location__filter" for="StLocationFilter-{{ suffix }}">
        <span class="visually-hidden">{{ 'localization.find_country' | t }}</span>
        <input
          type="search"
          id="StLocationFilter-{{ suffix }}"
          class="st-location__filter-input"
          placeholder="{{ 'localization.find_country' | t }}"
          autocomplete="off"
          autocorrect="off"
          autocapitalize="off"
          spellcheck="false"
          data-location-filter
        >
      </label>
      <ul class="st-location__countries" role="list">
        {%- for c in localization.available_countries -%}
          {%- unless named contains c.iso_code -%}
            <li class="st-location__item" data-location-item data-name="{{ c.name | downcase | escape }} {{ c.iso_code | downcase }}">
              <button
                type="button"
                class="st-location__country{% if c.iso_code == current_iso %} is-current{% endif %}"
                data-location-pick="{{ c.iso_code }}"
                data-market="{{ c.market.handle }}"
                {% if c.iso_code == current_iso %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
              >{{ c.name }}</button>
            </li>
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
      <p class="st-location__none" data-location-none hidden>{{ 'localization.no_match' | t }}</p>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
